WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.073 --> 00:00:02.520
- Well, your son's name is Daniel.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.990
So did you name him after
your "Karate Kid" character?

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:06.470
Please say yes.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.028
- I don't know why you
draw that conclusion.

00:00:09.028 --> 00:00:10.553
(laughter)

00:00:10.553 --> 00:00:13.810
I mean, I never thought
of that till this...

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.850
Well, you know what?
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.303
Oh, here we are out in the
east end of Long Island.

00:00:18.303 --> 00:00:21.280
Yep, these shots are unbelievable.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.327
You can't... Everything is out there.

00:00:23.327 --> 00:00:25.503
(laughing)

00:00:25.503 --> 00:00:28.640
My wife's best friend growing
up was her cousin Daniel.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.080
So she always had an
affinity for that name,

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.670
and it was a classic Biblical
name that I always loved.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:37.440
I mean the "Karate Kid's"
character initially in the script

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.610
was Danny Weber, and when they cast me,

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.940
they added more vowels
to make him Italian.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.140
I don't know where that
came from, and on top of it,

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.900
the Daniel was something
I was steadfast on.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.330
So I always loved the name,
and it meant something to her.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.080
It was like is it too
soon? Should we name?

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.243
Will he have to care? Would this be good?

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:01.070
And we went for it, and I still
think it's a beautiful name.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.080
He's proud of it.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.223
Maybe a couple of years, he was
like, "Dad, did you have to?

00:01:05.223 --> 00:01:06.750
Did you really?" (laughter)

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.070
But now he's Dan, and he's his own.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.593
It's wonderful, it's wonderful.

00:01:10.593 --> 00:01:13.410
- I think it's really
cool. I think it's sweet.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.810
Did you get to keep anything
from the original movie?

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.790
I saw you took the
guitar from "Crossroads".

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.010
Did you take anything?

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.412
- Yeah, I take stuff, I take stuff.

00:01:20.412 --> 00:01:21.573
- [Kelly] Yeah, I like it.

00:01:21.573 --> 00:01:23.810
- I took the can of tuna
from "My Cousin Vinny."

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:24.923
That's... I won't open it.

00:01:24.923 --> 00:01:28.063
- I love "My Cousin Vinny"! Oh my God!

00:01:29.827 --> 00:01:31.690
- "The Karate Kid", I had
more than a few things.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.770
I got the '47 Ford convertible,

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.685
which I did not bring with me.

00:01:35.685 --> 00:01:37.160
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.750
- That's on the set of "Cobra Kai",

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.570
that photograph you're
looking at right now.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:44.490
And so, that is the original
car from the original film.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.920
And one of the things
that I did bring with me

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.720
is what is called a
hachimaki, which is basically

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:51.530
most people would say, "Oh, the headband."

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:55.010
But this is the original.
- [Kelly] Oh yeah.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.193
- The one I wore in the film.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.500
I mean, I wore a few of
them, but I kept this one.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.663
And there you go.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.160
What's interesting about it

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.350
is it wasn't necessarily an
early part of the script.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.460
It was in a rehearsal with Pat Morita

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:13.100
that he had this sort of
handkerchief he would use,

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.440
and this was it.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:17.190
And you know, he would
say, "This is a hachimaki."

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:20.630
And he spoke of the
Japanese-American culture

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:22.940
and in this case, Okinawan culture,

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:26.530
and what it meant when a
teacher gifts one to his student

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:31.530
and the, you know, the weight
and respect that is given

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:34.600
and when one is handed to the next.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.290
And I love all those types of traditions.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.000
So we try to carry that forward

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.510
in the "Cobra Kai" series as well.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.600
It's important to have those
Miyagi-isms ringing true

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.050
throughout the series, you know?

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:47.090
- Yeah. I loved it.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.310
I don't even remember what it's called,

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.320
but I remember I had one of the things

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:51.543
that was like doo-doo-doo-doo,
and the little things would-

00:02:51.543 --> 00:02:53.884
- Oh, the drum.
- The drum, yeah.

00:02:53.884 --> 00:02:55.400
I would be in my room,

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.030
and I'd be like, "This is
my moment. I'm about to..."

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.800
I mean, I was so weird,
and I loved that thing.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:00.633
(laughter)

